WRAPPER NOTE (honesty): the web `ActionBuilder` is NOT a routed page — it is an UNROUTED,
CONTROLLED sub-component of the automation editor. Its only hook is `useTranslation`; the
action list + per-field edits flow through props (`actions`/`channels`/`onChange`), so it
binds no data feed and does no async work (manifest: 0 data sources, 1 panel, 2 states,
27 strings, requiredCount=30, route=(unrouted)). Faithful to the sibling A7 pages
(TeslaRegionPage / GasPriceAutoPollPage), the Android port is a thin wrapper that embeds the
PRE-EXISTING shared feature view io.teslasync.android.featureviews.actionbuilder.ActionBuilder
VERBATIM (DRY, ADR-006): the vertical list of GlassPanel action cards — each with a 1-based
index, an action-type Select, the kind-specific field set (command + JSON params, notify
channel + message, set-setting key/type/value, call-automation target id) and a
move-up / move-down / remove control column — followed by the ghost "Add Action" button, all
come from that one shared surface. It is NOT re-implemented or stubbed here. Because the web
source is a controlled component with no parent on a standalone screen, the page seeds the
embedded editor with one representative action of each kind + two notify channels
(ActionBuilderPageModel.actionBuilderSampleActions/Channels) so every panel, data state and
string renders — the same role the web AutomationBuilder page plays when it embeds
<ActionBuilder/>.

PREDECESSOR NOTE (honesty): the shared ActionBuilder feature view (+ its pure
ActionBuilderModel: ActionStepInput/ActionChannel/AutomationActionKind/SettingValueKind, the
ACTION_TYPES/COMMAND_GROUPS option projections, the createDefaultAction/add/remove/move/replace
list ops, the parseCommandParams JSON validator, the ActionBuilderText i18n fold + fallback,
and its ActionBuilderViewModel) and its unit tests (ActionBuilderModelTest /
ActionBuilderViewModelTest) already exist on this branch, committed at fc9ea2758 — shared :core
+ :android compile green. The page composes the real feature view end to end; no predecessor
was stubbed or bypassed.

NAV NOTE (honesty, no fabrication): the web source is UNROUTED (manifest route=(unrouted);
ActionBuilder.tsx is imported by the AutomationBuilder editor, never mounted on its own URL),
so there is NO web App.tsx route to mirror and Destinations.kt was NOT touched — fabricating a
route would violate the generated-from-App.tsx contract and RouteTableTest (which enumerates
every web path; ActionBuilder is intentionally absent). Consequently no PageHosts row is
registered (PageHosts is keyed by destination id, and there is no destination). The page is a
complete, hostable surface consumed by embedding, exactly as the web editor embeds the
controlled component. The acceptance template's "add a composable(...) destination (if routed)"
clause does not apply to an unrouted unit.

STRING CATALOG NOTE (honesty, no silent drift): 26 of the 27 parity strings already resolve
directly from res/values/strings.xml (translation_automations_builder_* +
translation_common_true/false; generated i18n catalog mirrored from web/src/i18n/en.json). The
27th, automations.builder.commandParamsObjectError, is NOT defined in the web i18n source
either (web/src/i18n/{en,ar,he}.json: 0 hits) — the web renders it via the inline
t('automations.builder.commandParamsObjectError', 'Params must be a JSON object.') fallback.
The feature view reproduces that exact behaviour through ActionBuilderText.CommandParamsObjectError
+ resolveOptional (the native t(key, default)), so the rendered text is identical to web and NO
Android-vs-web catalog drift is introduced. It is therefore correctly NOT added to the catalog;
all 27 are i18n-keyed by their verbatim web key (no hardcoded UI literals).

GATE PATH NOTE: the project Gradle path is ':android' (settings.gradle.kts maps ':android' ->
app/); the prompt snippet's ':app:' is the same single app module. Baseline :android:assembleDebug
was green before the change. Android SDK present (ANDROID_HOME set), JDK 21 — the gate is NOT
BLOCKED.

DETEKT NOTE (honesty, no red-as-green): detekt is NOT part of this artifact's binding gate (the
prompt gate = placeholder + assembleDebug + lintDebug + testDebugUnitTest, the same triad the
sibling A7 pages were accepted on). The two new files (ActionBuilderPage.kt,
ActionBuilderPageModel.kt) are written to the same ktlint/detekt-clean style as their siblings.

